        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 21:34:04.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-18938 osd-ldiskfs: limit space waiting to be freed",
        "message": "LU-18938 osd-ldiskfs: limit space waiting to be freed\n\nA destroyed object larger than osd-ldiskfs.delayed_unlink_mb\nis freed in the background, so the OST thread destroying it\ndoes not wait for the truncate. Counting such objects does not bound\nthe work they leave behind, which grows with their size, and\nuntil it is done the space shows as used.\n\nTrack the space of the objects waiting to be freed on each\ndevice, and defer no more once it passes\nosd-ldiskfs.delayed_unlink_max_mb (256 GiB by default): the\ndestroying thread then frees the object itself, which slows\ndestroys down to the rate the space is released.\nosd-ldiskfs.*.delayed_unlink_pending_mb shows the space waiting.\n\nFixes: 444d29c21891 (\"LU-18938 obdclass: delay an object free\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id89673683075eeb1198df0b4a1e6124371b703f1\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
